# Phase:        pre
# Target:       security/src/budget/report.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        equiv-rewrite
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 18: aeneas rejects a loop that
#               reassigns a borrow-carrying value, and one that runs while such
#               a value is borrowed.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: `binding_index` and `first_minimum` are
#               compiled but unused there. In the extracted variant,
#               `binding_term` returns the term at the position of the first
#               minimum of the seven bit counts.
# Upstreamable: no: the term-copying loop is the natural Rust.
# Drop when:    aeneas supports loops over borrow-carrying values.
# Test:         test p3-security --lib pre_patch_020
# Mutation:     `first_minimum` keeps the last minimum on a tie, so it disagrees
#               with `binding_term` and the differential test fails.
#
# `binding_term` keeps a running `SecurityTerm` (which holds a `&'static str`)
# and reassigns it in a loop; aeneas cannot translate that loop.
# `first_minimum` runs the same loop over the seven `u64` bit counts, and
# `binding_index` feeds it, both compiled in every build. Under
# cfg(hax_backend_lean) `binding_term` returns `self.terms[self.binding_index()]`.
# Ties resolve to the earliest round in both. The differential test compares
# the two on 20000 reports, half of them with values in 0..4 to force ties.
#
